{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    "testFramework": "testo",
    // `composer mutation` counts uncovered code (--with-uncovered): 2299
    // mutants, 42 of them dropped by the signature-default regex below.
    // Everything that can be observed is killed (see tests/); what is left
    // is listed here, each entry with the reasoning that makes it
    // unkillable. No ignores: Infection still generates and runs every one
    // of them, this is a record, not a suppression. The 4 Not Covered
    // entries are in the same class (no behaviour to observe, or no safe way
    // to reach the line).
    //
    // A. Output-neutral rewrites of an array/list:
    //    - Doctor/McpDoctor.php:205 UnwrapArrayValues (`array_values(
    //      array_unique($features))` -> `array_unique($features)`): the only
    //      consumer is `implode(', ', $features)`, which ignores keys. The
    //      sibling UnwrapArrayUnique IS killed (a feature required twice for
    //      one service is listed once).
    //    - Identity/StaticSecretResolver.php:52 UnwrapArrayValues: $list is
    //      only iterated, never indexed, and nothing exposes it.
    //    - OpenApi/OperationRequestBuilder.php:307 UnwrapArrayValues: the
    //      values are counted and iterated into a fresh list; keys never read.
    //    - Session/PrivateFileSessionStore.php:78 UnwrapArrayValues (Not
    //      Covered): the SDK's FileSessionStore::gc() already returns a list.
    //
    // B. Array-key coercion: OpenApi/OperationRequestBuilder.php:122
    //    CastString x2 (`$styleOverrides[(string) $operationId]
    //    [(string) $parameterName]`): PHP turns a numeric-string key into the
    //    int key anyway, so the cast changes nothing a lookup can see.
    //
    // C. Parameter of a call that cannot influence the result:
    //    - Doctor/McpDoctor.php:121 IncrementInteger (`explode(':', $h, 2)[0]`
    //      -> limit 3): index [0] is the text before the FIRST separator for
    //      any limit >= 2.
    //    - Utf8.php:55 DecrementInteger (`default => 1` -> 0): reached only
    //      for an ASCII lead byte, where `strlen($cut) - $index` is >= 1, so
    //      `>= 0` and `>= 1` are both always true.
    //    - Interceptor/ResponseSizeLimitInterceptor.php:63 LessThanOrEqualTo:
    //      at $size === $maxBytes Utf8::cut() returns its input untouched
    //      (its own first line is `strlen <= max`), so $kept is the same.
    //    - McpServerFactory.php:377 PlusEqual (`$registered += n` -> `-=`):
    //      every term is >= 0, so only `=== 0` is read, and it is the same
    //      for the negated sum.
    //
    // D. `?? 0` fallback read by a `> 0` guard, mutated to `?? -1`: the
    //    fallback only fires when the params key is absent, and the next
    //    statement tells 0 from -1 not at all (both disable the feature).
    //    The `?? 1` siblings and `cache_ttl ?? -1` ARE killed:
    //    - McpServerComponentResolver.php:196 DecrementInteger (budget calls)
    //    - McpServerComponentResolver.php:234 DecrementInteger (tool_result_bytes)
    //
    // E. Guards whose removal leaves the same value behind a PHP warning are
    //    killed by tests that turn warnings into exceptions (WarningsAsErrors):
    //    McpAction ownedBy/stampOwner, SpecIndex tags/required,
    //    SpecLoader::readCache, PromptFile::parseArguments,
    //    DeclarativeToolVisibility::tagsOf and compile. What remains is the
    //    warning-free form of the same shape (a chain of `?? null` over an
    //    empty array, or an early `return` in front of code that degrades to
    //    the same result):
    //    - OpenApi/SpecIndex.php:298 ReturnRemoval (extractRequestBodySchema:
    //      `$body === []` -> null; every following `?? null` converges on null)
    //    - McpListCommand.php:178 ReturnRemoval (arguments(): a non-array
    //      schema renders '' with or without the early return)
    //    - CompactToolResultFormatter.php:68 ReturnRemoval (an empty array
    //      falls through to json_encode([]) === '[]', the same TextContent)
    //
    // F. Branches the constructor/factory invariants make unreachable:
    //    - OpenApi/OperationRequestBuilder.php:246 LogicalAnd (`identity &&
    //      delegated` -> `||`): the constructor rejects configuring exactly
    //      one of the two, so only "both" and "neither" exist.
    //    - OpenApi/OpenApiBridgeFactory.php:185, :186 Throw_ (the twins of the
    //      guards in create(), which rejects a URL spec without a client or a
    //      request factory before index() is reached).
    //    - McpServerFactory.php:251 LogicalOrAllSubExprNegation: installing the
    //      pass-through reference handler with nothing configured is
    //      behaviourally identical to not installing it.
    //
    // G. Text built from a closed set / regex shape:
    //    - OpenApi/SpecIndex.php:275 Concat x2, ConcatOperandRemoval
    //      (`$in . ':' . $name`): $in is one of path/query/header/cookie, four
    //      DISTINCT first characters in the fixed prefix position, so no
    //      separator choice can make two different parameters collide.
    //    - Prompts/PromptFile.php:53 PregMatchRemoveDollar: the trailing `$`
    //      follows a greedy `(.*)` under /s, which reaches the end anyway.
    //    - Prompts/PromptFile.php:65 Throw_ (Not Covered): needs an empty
    //      basename for a readable file, which no portable path produces.
    //
    // H. Testing/McpTester.php: it speaks to a real SDK server, and several
    //    mutants touch what that server never reacts to:
    //    - :168 TrueValue (`$seenCursors[$cursor] = true` -> false): only
    //      isset() reads the map, and isset() is true for a stored false.
    //    - :235 ArrayItemRemoval (`jsonrpc` dropped from the initialized
    //      notification): the SDK accepts the notification without it. The
    //      call itself IS killed (the server records the notification).
    //    - :295 LogicalAnd (`isset($decoded['error']) && is_array(...)`):
    //      differs only for a non-array `error`, which no SDK handler can
    //      produce (Error always serializes to an object).
    //    - :289 ReturnRemoval (Not Covered): an empty body answers a request
    //      only for a notification, and request() always sends an id.
    //
    // I. OutputBufferReleasingStream.php:136 ReturnRemoval (Not Covered):
    //    `return` when a buffer refuses to be removed. The mutant spins
    //    forever, and the test would have to leave a non-removable output
    //    buffer in the shared test process.
    //
    // J. 5.0 (SDK 0.10, OAuth):
    //    - OAuth/OAuthComponentFactory.php:141 Throw_ (`firebase/php-jwt`
    //      missing): the library is a dev dependency, so the class always
    //      exists in the test process; without it the SDK would fail later
    //      with a class-not-found error, the message is the only difference.
    //    - ToolResultTextFormatter.php:77 ReturnRemoval (`[]` -> `'[]'`
    //      text): the general path ends in `json_encode([])`, which is the
    //      same `'[]'`. Kept as a branch only to mirror the SDK's
    //      ToolResultFormatter::format() line for line.
    //
    // Mutants that are only ever "Timed Out" are infinite loops/recursion by
    // construction (Utf8 backing-over loop, McpTester::listAll() do-while,
    // JsonPointerResolver depth/node budget, the bounded stream readers fed an
    // endless body): the original code is what stops them, nothing else can.
    // Unit only: every package declares a Benchmarks suite (testo.php), and Infection's initial
    // test run would execute it. A timing-sensitive benchmark fails under host load and aborts
    // the whole mutation run (result, 2026-11-03). Benchmarks mutate nothing and kill nothing.
    "testFrameworkOptions": "--suite=Unit",
    "minMsi": 97,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true,
        // Constructor/method parameter declarations with a default value
        // (`private int $x = 100,`, `bool $strict = false,`): the mutant sits on a
        // signature line with no executable opcode under pcov, so it is reported Not
        // Covered whatever the tests do. Only a type-prefixed `$name = default,` line
        // matches; a body line cannot (no type before the variable). Do NOT add ^ or $:
        // Infection wraps the pattern as ^-\s*REGEX$ over the removed diff line.
        // Verified 2026-11-01 by diffing the survivor lists with and without it:
        // bulkhead 6, circuit-breaker 13, json-ld 19 mutants removed, all of them
        // such signature lines; Escaped and Timed Out unchanged.
        "global-ignoreSourceCodeByRegex": [
            "(?:(?:private|protected|public|readonly)\\s+)*\\??[A-Za-z_\\\\][\\w\\\\|]*\\s+\\$\\w+\\s*=\\s*[^,;]+,"
        ],
        // Off: with --with-uncovered a PublicVisibility mutant sits on a parameterless
        // method's signature line, which has no executable opcode under pcov/xdebug,
        // so it is reported Not Covered and can never be killed, whatever #[Covers]
        // says. Measured on pinned-http-client 2026-11-01: 4 of 4 such mutants were
        // Not Covered, none killed.
        "PublicVisibility": false,
        // Off for the same reason: a ProtectedVisibility mutant on a protected method's
        // signature line is Not Covered and cannot be killed. Measured on
        // understudy-phpunit 2026-11-01: 4 of 4 such mutants were Not Covered.
        "ProtectedVisibility": false
    }
}
